rong; also the HT reference is included to show how variable a design-based estimator is at this sample size\n  - evidence: paper.tex Results (HT paragraph says it was not logged and is evidently dominated by noise or by the cap); paper.tex Discussion paragraph 2; paper_data.json final_evaluation.metrics.baseline_ht_rmse_rel=0.9938 with no HT variance or bias decomposition; claims_grounding.json has only the 0.994 value for HT; evaluate_final.py baseline_ht (terms are zero for units outside fully treated or control neighbourhoods); evaluation_evidence candidate_diagnostics_trust=unverified.\n  - requested_fix: Replace the Discussion sentence with a qualified one, e.g. that HT scored 0.994 mean relative RMSE here, that the cause (variance, sparsity of fully exposed units, or the cap) was not diagnosed, and that regression errors were larger in cases 6-8 without verification of the cause. In Related Work drop the claim that HT is included to show variability.\n- `related-work-beyond-title-grounding` (Related Work; Introduction; Reliability): claims_grounding.json states related-work statements cite works by title/topic only, and references_provenance.json holds only titles, years and ids with no abstracts. The titles do not support these content-level details (linear-model analysis, covariate-selection scheme, block bootstrap, cluster-robust variance in Aronow).\n  - claim: Chin2018RegressionAF analyzed it under linear models; Han2023ModelbasedRA select graph-based and treatment-based covariates for the regression and use block bootstrap intervals; Cluster-robust and network-aware variance estimation is a developed topic (Aronow2013EstimatingAC, Han2023ModelbasedRA); block-bootstrap intervals for regression adjustment\n  - evidence: claims_grounding.json claim on related-work statements (\"cite only works by title/topic\"); references_provenance.json entries for Chin2018RegressionAF (\"Regression Adjustments for Estimating the Global Treatment Effect in Experiments with Interference\"), Han2023ModelbasedRA (\"Model-based regression adjustment with model-free covariates for network interference\") and Aronow2013EstimatingAC (no abstract fields).\n  - requested_fix: Reduce these sentences to title-level descriptions (e.g. Han et al. propose model-based regression adjustment for network interference, Chin studies regression adjustments for the global treatment effect). Remove the linear-model, covariate-selection, block-bootstrap and cluster-robust attributions, or cite them as unverified recollection.\n- `seed-gap-and-control-overinterpretation` (Results (Reliability, Validity checks); Supplementary Negative Controls and Fallbacks): The gap between the mean of per-seed errors and the plane RMSE is attributed to case 8, but the paper states per-case decomposition for seeds is unavailable, so the attribution is unsupported. The constant-outcome control only shows the estimate was about 9.0e-15. That is not the exact 0 stated in the Fallbacks paragraph, and the control does not support a conclusion about spurious covariate or exposure effects in general.\n  - claim: the per-seed mean 0.102 is below the RMSE aggregate of 0.126 because RMSE weights large errors such as those in case 8; The constant-outcome control rules out spurious effects from the covariate and exposure terms; a constant outcome returns the estimate 0\n  - evidence: derived_stats.json (seed_mean 0.1015, case_mean_of_8 0.1264, no per-case per-seed data); paper_data.json final_evaluation.metrics.control_constant_max_abs_est=9.008e-15; paper.tex statement that per-case decomposition for seeds is not available; frozen_estimator/program.py returns exactly 0.0 only when var(y)==0.\n  - requested_fix: State only that the mean absolute per-seed error is lower than the RMSE aggregate, without attributing the gap to case 8. Describe the constant-outcome result as an estimate of magnitude about 9e-15 (numerically zero) and drop the claim that it rules out spurious effects. In the Fallbacks paragraph say the constant-outcome branch returns 0 when the outcome variance is exactly zero.\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[0].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\n- figures[1].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 1636 < 2400\n- figures[2] exceeds category budget in panel 0: 24 > 3\n- figures[2].font_sizes.title below minimum: 9.0 < 10.0\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1486 < 2400\nfigures:\nmain_accuracy.pdf\nmain_accuracy.png\nmain_accuracy.png.prov.json\noverview_schematic.png\noverview_schematic.png.prov.json\noverview_schematic.prompts.json\nreliability.pdf\nreliability.png\nreliability.png.prov.json\n\nscientific-evidence:\nbundle.manifest.json\nledger.jsonl\nschemas\nspec.md\nverification-report.json\n\nsource_evidence:\nestimator_01\nestimator_02\nevaluator\nfrozen_estimator","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92f14c43-e077-40f1-8a98-2a7fca78a5c1","uuid":"25f35e82-bdc0-4fc8-beb0-9e7ede1b5153","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:51:10.543Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 10940\ndrwx------ 8 agent agent    4096 Nov 11 08:51 .\ndrwx------ 9 agent agent    4096 Nov 11 08:43 ..\n-rw------- 1 agent agent     751 Nov 11 08:12 .agentic_paper_workspace.json\ndrwx------ 3 agent agent    4096 Nov 11 08:12 .claude\n-rw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov 11 08:48 .concept_figure_complete\nprw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov 11 08:51 .paper_repair_round_2_stream_20261111_081253.fifo\n-rw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov 11 08:12 .paper_two_stage_enabled\n-rw------- 1 agent agent       0 Nov 11 08:35 .postdraft_reference_enrichment_complete\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    3685 Nov 11 08:51 VENUE.md\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent    7719 Nov 11 08:46 build_figures.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent   10848 Nov 11 08:47 claims_grounding.json\n-rw------- 1 agent agent    5610 Nov 11 08:43 concept_figure_run.log\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     975 Nov 11 08:46 derived_stats.json\n-rw-r--r-- 1 agent agent     