{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JZRaN3Kxe8efxCJQZ15XRr","type":"tool_result","content":"\\end{figure}\nPer-seed errors (Figure~\\ref{fig:rel}a) have a mean of 0.102 with bootstrap interval [0.093, 0.113]; % @evidence[[derived_stats.json#seed_mean]]\n this is the mean absolute relative error over cases, which is below the RMSE aggregate of 0.126 because RMSE weights large errors such as those in case 8. Two seeds stand out (9001 and 9015, with per-seed errors 0.180 and 0.173), while every other seed lies between 0.078 and 0.119; % @evidence[[derived_stats.json#outlier_seeds]]\n excluding them the mean is 0.095. % @evidence[[derived_stats.json#mean_excluding_outliers]]\n Per-case decomposition for those seeds is not available, so we do not know which case drove them.\n\\end{tabular}\n\\end{table}\nThe constant-outcome control rules out spurious effects from the covariate and exposure terms, the permuted-outcome control gives a mean absolute estimate of 0.059 times the true GATE, and the relabelled-graph error (0.627) is far above the headline error of 0.126 and similar to the difference-in-means value. We make no mechanistic claim from these values. None of these supports accuracy on its own.\n\n19:plt.rcParams.update({\"font.size\": 8, \"axes.labelsize\": 8, \"axes.titlesize\": 8,\n20:                     \"xtick.labelsize\": 7, \"ytick.labelsize\": 7, \"legend.fontsize\": 7,\n62:    fig.savefig(FIG / f\"{name}.pdf\", bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n63:    fig.savefig(FIG / f\"{name}.png\", dpi=300, bbox_inches=\"tight\")\n71:fig, (a, b) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(5.5, 2.8), gridspec_kw={\"width_ratios\": [1, 1.55]})\n78:    a.text(i, v * 1.05, f\"{v:.3f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=7)\n87:    b.text(i, v + 0.008, f\"{v:.3f}\", ha=\"center\", va=\"bottom\", fontsize=7)\n90:b.set_xticks(range(8)); b.set_xticklabels(cases, fontsize=7)\n97:fig, (a, b) = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(5.0, 2.6), gridspec_kw={\"width_ratios\": [1.7, 1]})\n101:        a.annotate(str(s), (s, v), textcoords=\"offset points\", xytext=(0, 6), ha=\"center\", fontsize=7)\n109:b.axhline(0.95, color=\"crimson\", ls=\"--\", lw=1.2); b.text(-0.45, 0.97, \"nominal 0.95\", color=\"crimson\", ha=\"left\", fontsize=7)\n110:b.text(0, M[\"ci_coverage\"] - 0.06, f\"{M['ci_coverage']:.3f}\", ha=\"center\", color=\"w\", fontsize=7)\n111:b.text(0, 0.05, f\"rel. width\\n{M['ci_width_rel']:.3f}\", ha=\"center\", color=\"w\", fontsize=7)\n124:    if p.exists() and p.stat().st_size > 2:\n126:    fig = plt.figure(figsize=(7, 2.6)); fig.text(0.5, 0.5, \"overview_schematic (placeholder)\", ha=\"center\")\n127:    fig.savefig(FIG / \"overview_schematic.png\", dpi=200); plt.close(fig)\n{\n \"schema_name\": \"scientific-evidence.artifact-manifest\",\n \"artifact\": {\n  \"path\": \"figures/reliability.png\",\n  \"kind\": \"figure\"\n },\n \"derived_from\": [\n  \"@evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\",\n  \"@evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.metrics]]\",\n  \"@evidence[[build_figures.py]]\"\n ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"92f14c43-e077-40f1-8a98-2a7fca78a5c1","uuid":"45a510af-c291-45c8-9539-c6521e8375f5","timestamp":"2026-11-11T08:51:17.269Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"\\end{figure}\nPer-seed errors (Figure~\\ref{fig:rel}a) have a mean of 0.102 with bootstrap interval [0.093, 0.113]; % @evidence[[derived_stats.json#seed_mean]]\n this is the mean absolute relative error over cases, which is below the RMSE aggregate of 0.126 because RMSE weights large errors such as those in case 8. Two seeds stand out (9001 and 9015, with per-seed errors 0.180 and 0.173), while every other seed lies between 0.078 and 0.119; % @evidence[[derived_stats.json#outlier_seeds]]\n excluding them the mean is 0.095. % @evidence[[derived_stats.json#mean_excluding_outliers]]\n Per-case decomposition for those seeds is not available, so we do not know which case drove them.\n\\e