I fixed the three audit findings and the two figure-manifest errors in `paper.tex`. The paper compiles at 15 pages, with the body at 9 pages, and the evidence verifier reports 0 dangling references (71 total).

I couldn't run `validate_figures.py` (it needs the orchestrator's `src` package). I also couldn't run the repo's `compile_latex.sh` (`pdftotext` is missing), so I compiled with plain `pdflatex` and `bibtex` instead. I didn't re-run the agentic evidence audit itself, so I don't know that it now passes.

**Audit fixes**
- **HT overclaim:** the paper now reports the Horvitz–Thompson (HT) score of 0.994 and says its cause is undiagnosed (variance, sparsity of fully exposed neighbourhoods, or the error cap). I removed the "variance was prohibitive" sentence, the "HT is included to show variability" wording, and the claim that regression error was large only when the mapping was wrong. The Discussion sentence now says regression errors were larger in cases 6–8 without a verified cause.
- **Related work:** Chin, Han and Aronow are described at title level only. I removed the attributions to linear-model analysis, covariate selection, block bootstrap and cluster-robust variance.
- **Seed gap and controls:** I removed the claim that the per-seed mean sits below the RMSE aggregate because of case 8. The constant-outcome control is now described as about 9×10⁻¹⁵ (numerically zero), with no "rules out spurious effects" claim. The fallback text now says the estimate is 0 only when outcome variance is exactly zero.

**Figure fixes**
- I set the manifest `figure_type` values to `bar_two_panel` and `strip_plus_bar` to match the strategy. I also set the manifest title font size to 10 and the reliability panel category count to 1.
- I regenerated the two matplotlib figures at 500 dpi, so they are now 2727 px and 2482 px wide, above the 2400 px minimum. I moved the reliability legend off the "9015" label and set the axis titles to 10 pt.
- The overview schematic was left alone.

**Page budget**
The body spilled onto page 10, so I trimmed some prose to bring it back to 9 pages. That cut the Wager/Ting regression-adjustment sentence, which leaves 28 cited keys, still above the minimum of 25. It also shortened parts of the Discussion and the Conclusion's next-steps sentence.

I appended this round to `memory.md`, `global_memory/memory.md` and `global_memory/memory.jsonl`.
